{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Then you shall fear.</b> The meaning: when the kings come to you and bring your sons, then you shall fear like a person who is frightened when salvation comes to him and a thing that never entered his heart, as when one is called upon to find a lost object." "<b>ונהרת.</b> Flow here and there." "<b>And fear.</b> And behold, there shall be fear mixed with joy, and this is \"your heart shall enlarge,\" the opposite of distress." "<b>For the wealth of the sea shall be turned upon you.</b> Or the meaning of \"you shall fear\" is because of the great multitude that shall be turned upon you." "<b>Wealth of the nations.</b> On dry land."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:25.005258172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}